 ## Background
-AR-NeRF was proposed to address the inconsistency between PE frequency regularization and rendering loss in few-shot NeRF, which prevents high-quality novel view synthesis [S1]. It builds on prior work like FreeNeRF and SPARF that regularize PE frequency [S1]. The method was introduced in "Few-shot NeRF by Adaptive Rendering Loss Regularization" [S1].
+AR-NeRF was proposed to address the inconsistency between Positional Encoding (PE) frequency regularization and rendering loss in few-shot NeRF settings [S1]. It builds on the observation that high-frequency PEs can cause early overfitting to local details, preventing the learning of global structures [S1]. The method was introduced by Xu et al. [S1].
 
